  "notes": "{心酔|しんすい} describes a state of being deeply captivated or devoted to something. The character {酔|すい} (intoxicated) suggests being 'drunk' with admiration.\n\nUSAGE:\n- Often used with ⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧ to indicate what one is captivated by\n- Can have a slightly negative nuance of being blindly devoted\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {傾倒|けいとう}: devotion, admiration\n- ⟦{夢中|むちゅう}→夢中：03752_muchuu⟧: being absorbed in\n- ⟦{盲信|もうしん}→盲信：09239_moushin⟧: blind faith (more negative)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- X⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{心酔|しんすい}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to be captivated by X\n- {心酔|しんすい}⟦{者|しゃ}→〜者：04662_sha⟧: an admirer, devotee",
